ed at Sea.\", <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Times\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:New York Times\">New York Times</a></i>, Wednesday, February 26, 1873, page 2, citing the <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Post\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Boston Post\">Boston Post</a></i> of February 24, 1873. Retrieved on June 19, 2008.\n</p>\nFirst sentence: \"It is now believed that the fine brig <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Celeste\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Mary Celeste\">Mary Celeste</a>, of about 236 tons, commanded by Capt. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Briggs\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Benjamin Briggs\">Benjamin Briggs</a>, of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marion,_Massachusetts\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Marion, Massachusetts\">Marion, Mass.</a>, was seized by pirates in the latter part of November, and that, after murdering the Captain, his wife, child, and officers, the vessel was abandoned near the Western Islands, where the miscreants are supposed to have landed.\"","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1873-02-24","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:MaryCeleste_1873February26.gif\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:File:MaryCeleste 1873February26.gif\">en:File:MaryCeleste 1873February26.gif</a> uploaded <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Richard_Arthur_Norton_(1958-_)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:User:Richard Arthur Norton (1958- )\">en:User:Richard Arthur Norton (1958- )</a>, <br>possibly from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://query.nytimes.com/gst/abstract.html?res=9A04E6DA1539EF34BC4E51DFB4668388669FDE\" href=\"https://query.nytimes.com/gst/abstract.html?res=9A04E6DA1539EF34BC4E51DFB4668388669FDE\">http://query.nytimes.com/gst/abstract.html?res=9A04E6DA1539EF34BC4E51DFB4668388669FDE</a><br>from \n</p>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original